A little late, but I've had a chance to figure out what I did and how
I got there:

Ok, so it's only a dwarven valk, but it's a first ascension
nonetheless:

Found some tripe on DL2 that kept Jeeves fed and happy, got a +0 t-
shirt early on.  Jeeves liked a ring I found, and it turned out to be
+1 protection which I was happy to use in the early game.  Found a
lamp on DL3 and my first bit of poison resistance from a shrieker soon
after, and headed down the mines.  Silver saber, small bag and of
course daggers aplenty, all in the early mines.

Was at XL 6 when I reached DL 6, and a jaguar spawned.  Gave me a bit
of a fright, but it turned into more food for Jeeves once I vanquished
it.

Spotted a watchman on DL7 - minetown, not orc town, thank Tyr.  Bought
4 food rations off a rip-off merchant Ogre because I didn't want to
risk starving and had nothing more to train Jeeves to carry with.
Izchak was a fellow dwarf, had a couple of oil lamps going cheap, I
checked - mine wasn't an oil lamp.  Wandered off to find the temple.
Cross-aligned, but I didn't mind too much because the magic lamp came
pre-blessed!

After wondering what awesome artifact to wish for (I don't usually get
wishes until there's already 3-4 artifacts created), I plumped for +3
GDSM, which I got.  Figured the AC would help me wherever the MR
couldn't.

An orc captain shot an 'extremely toxic' poisoned arrow at me -
would've been a YA(A|S)D in vanilla, but poison instadeath has been
removed in Spork.  Finally got an MC cloak (only orcish) off his
corpse though.  Ended up with a stethoscope from a tool shop, and took
a quick trip down past minetown and found 7 candles just lying on the
ground by the upstair.

Jeeves, sick of one-shotting gnomes, went after a watchman and felled
him, giving me +1 helmet and gloves.  A red naga spawned outside a
shop I was trying to coax Jeeves into - I killed it but the dog got to
the corpse before I could.  Got a towel from the death drop though.
Thankfully the gen store shopkeeper was human, so the prices looked
familiar and I could price-id with no trouble.

Found and identified a =3DoFA down the mines, and got a second magic
lamp that I kept as a light source.  Jeeves went after a white
unicorn, but lost.  Had a bit of close encounter with four fire ants -
had to dust-E to scare them off while I whacked 'em.  Got long sword
and dagger to skilled and decided to try two-weaponing with a nice
short elven dagger in the off hand, which worked relatively well on
weak monsters.

Had to pray after bumping into a gray fungus on my way back up the
mines.  Found a bag in an unexplored corner of the upper mines, but it
turned out to be tricks.  Decided to head for sokoban hoping for a
bigger bag, or reflection.  Found another t-shirt which turned out to
be +2.

Built a small stash at the downstair to the mines instead when I found
a handy chest.  Had my /oTele nicked by a nymph, who promptly wasted
all its charges running away from me.  A Lich scrollshop on DL5 left
me wishing I still had a pet and some way of raising its apport. 78zm
for an i.d. scroll? Sheesh! Turned around once I'd built my stash and
went back for the luckstone.

Lost a level to a foocubus, but hit a shrieker until i got it back.
Then went and got an extra level by consorting with another one I
found wandering around minetown.  Back to the stash to dump my latest
potions, as I still didn=92t have a unihorn.

Had a major scare wandering around the mines in the hopes of a cross-
aligned unicorn when a chameleon suddenly showed up as a purple L =96
but in a few moves it=92d become an ettin zombie, which I quickly
dispatched. Shortly after, a floating eye finally left a corpse I
could gobble.

Finally got a chance to clear out Mines=92 End (mimic version), though a
fire elemental took me to 5HP and no projectiles =96 had to throw junk I
picked up off the dungeon floor at it until I could sneak round it and
grab my dagger stack again.  Thank goodness for that speed intrinsic I
got at level 7!  Locked myself in a dead end room and put on the
=3DoRegen for a few turns. Phew.

Dragged myself up to minetown again, price-id on the luckstone and a
couple of scrolls (finally, at least ONE 80z scroll).  Decided it was
time to get to soko when I had to pray when my stomach started
rumbling.  Managed to kill and eat a grey unicorn on the way up,
though.

Soko was uneventful, got /oCancellation, and a cursed amulet in the
BoH (the rewards are treated as normal spawns in SporkHack - I've got
a cursed 2oR there before).  Still no altar except minetown, and I was
getting burdened again, so back I went.  Cancelled a cursed =93oESP on
the way, as well as some cursed boots and rings.  This included what
turned out to be a pair of speed boots.  Bingo!

Couldn't resist the smell of a fresh tengu corpse, and ended up with
teleportitis. D'oh!

Found a nymph-owned jewellery store on DL11, then completely forgot
about it until I zoomed past it on the ascension run.  Might not have
had to spend half the time polypiling for a =3DoLev had I gone back and
cleared it out at some point....

My first altar outside minetown was on DL12 =96 didn=92t even have to
convert it.  Quest was DL13, but I was only XL12 by then, so I just
grabbed a few fire (gi)ant corpses to munch on, and kept hunting round
for rings, hoping to get teleport control =96 but not before a hill
giant zapped me with a /oL=92nin=92 and broke a couple of wands and my
=3DoFA.

Back to the altar =96 created some holy water, blessed my unihorn, magic
lamp and BoH.  Soon after, a beehive found shortly after a prayer that
had restored my stats (plus a corpse that brought me to 100% poison
resistance) meant that I almost had respectable strength again.

Found a +3 elven helm on pretty much the first elf I saw, which meant
that at XL12 with no metal armour, force bolt was at (only) 50%
failure =96 hooray for starting with 7 int!

Actually physically yelped when a shambling horror read a scroll of
create monster on DL17 =96 10 bees, 3 ants, 2 jaguars, a footrice, 4
orcs and a handful of other monsters appeared.  Luckily burning E
works with most lower level monsters, so it wasn=92t a complete
disaster.  One of the orcs had been wielding ogresmasher, but I didn=92t
think it was worth wasting skill slots on unless I got gifted mojo.

Found a temple of Odin on DL18 after falling through a trapdoor on the
rogue level (15), and discovered a leprechaun hall (which are slightly
trickier in spork due to combat usually causing noise) on the way up:
5 points of protection.

Managed to corrode my long sword with a hallucinogen-distorted acid
blob.  Really don=92t like the lack of =91hallu=92 in the status line.  It=
=92s
a minor thing, though.  In the same sacfest, a swarm of fireants
proved that I=92d got to 100% fire res. A leprechaun obliged with a /
oPoly, but the only surefire way of price-iding scrolls was back in
minetown =96 so back I went.  Got a bit of a shock when a grey @ there
started to hit me with knives (I didn=92t want to be known as a
murderer!), but it was only a soldier.

Thought I=92d get a fooproof long sword off an aleax, but it turned out
to be carrying a silver mace named Demonbane.  Artifact no. 2. Damn,
should=92ve gone for 'Swandir earlier.  Oh well, presumably I=92d get
scalybur when I inevitably got crowned.

A minor polypiling session yielded a cloak of invisibility, and my god-
gifted +5 scale mail became much-wanted blessed fixed +3 leather
gloves (which I kept to the end).  Oh, I also got a blank spellbook as
a prayer gift along the way.

Converted another altar on DL 21. Demilich (in a zoo with 4 yellow Ls
as well) a level down burnt my speed boots, summoned a hill giant
shaman and a lot of stuff got cursed and my BoH unblessed. Eventually
beat them both off, and got two spellbooks for my trouble - repair
armour and one I couldn't read.  Two of the other liches were easy to
take care of; the other two set my shield and boots to completely
burnt before they were dispatched.

Fooproofed my speed boots before they could be whipped off my feet,
and swapped my shield for an elven dagger again, figuring my to-hit
might have gone up sufficiently to two-wep successfully by now.
Turned out to be good enough for elementals but not Olog-Hai. A
shambling horror on the way back to the stash got me to XL14, so I
looted the chest beside the Norn (cash & a spellbook), dumped what I
could  in the stash, and headed for the quest.

Ended up in a puddle on the quest after rushing along the ice with
uncontrolled teleportitis. (G and _ don't work on ice), but that was
the worst of it.  Surtur was a pushover. On way up, put on "oMB and
gobbled giant corpses until my strength was 18/95.  Got back to the
altar and ^T-tested my new rings - finally got teleport control.

Went after a centaur that had run off with the loot from a throne room
and ended up with 3 more points of protection.  Blessed some geno
scrolls and got rid of demi & arch liches, saving the second scroll
for later.

Arrived at medusa, grateful for the peaceful titan, but with no means
of crossing water.  Went back for another short polypiling session -
it's only been mildly nerfed for the casual polypiler, especially if
they have a means of cancelling anything that gets negative
enchantment.  Got jungle boots; didn't seem to be fumbling, jumping,
speed or kicking.  Didn't know if there were any other new magical
boots but I thought I'd dump my BoH and rustables and try to walk on
water.  Water walking boots it was.

Wandered across medusa, avoiding the electric eels. Just about caught
a gremlin as it opened the door onto the wet part of the level - he
only split 3 times or so.  Luckily none of the Ds were black, or I'd
have had to do some serious thinking.  Got gray dragon scales (already
had GDSM) and beat up an Aleax for a shield of reflection and a
blessed fixed longsword to replace my rusty corroded one. Perseus'
sack had a blessed ?oEW in it, which was nice. A troll chucked a
silver dagger at me and I thought 'Ooh, bet that'd be a nice off-hand
weapon for Hegemmon'.  I switched between shield of Reflection &
silver dagger as needed from then until I got the "oR later.

The level below medusa was my first lava level.  There was an orange
D, but I had sleep resistance by then, and nothing much else scary.
One /oCold zap bridged the 2-step lava flow separating > from <.

The castle had 2 arch-liches so I ran away and geno'd L again with the
other blessed scroll.  Put on my water walking boots and wandered to
the back door, killing xorns as necessary, and promply fell down to
the VoTD.  Spork has stairs down from the castle, so I read a ?oE and
plugged the holes.  No decent weapons or armour in the back rooms, and
the 2 yellow, 1 silver, 1 orange dragon yielded orange scales that I
kept in case I got another MR source.

Killed a lot of stuff in the castle. The /oWishing was in the second
box I checked, decided to go for "oReflection so I could two-weap all
the time, and then cursed myself and hoped the wand wasn't (0:1).
Thankfully, it was (0:3).  Wished for a marker as a follow up.

Went back to the stash, made some holy water, wrote a couple of
scrolls, blessed my !oFH, alchemised some diluted !oEH (later found !
oGE and quaffed diluted !oFH to take maxHP to 200). A lurker on the
way to the fountain to dilute and merge my !oEH dropped a can of
grease. Score! Wished up 2 more markers. Ended up with a 6 long sword,
+6 silver dagger, and a stack of +7 elven daggers.
T-shirt, GDSM, speed boots, elven helm, gloves and (still) [oInvis and
8 points of protection gave me a total AC of -38. Wandered off to
gehennom without my candles, dolt that I am.  Also no source of
levitation yet - the ring shop I'd left for later would've been one
level above the altar stash, if only I'd looked!

Magic eyes floating out into lava turned out to be very annoying -
didn't want to waste my highly enchanted projectiles, and kept missing
with wands (possibly because I had my blindfold on, but I'm not sure
the code takes that into account if you have telepathy).

Found Dragonbane lying in the VoTD, so that meant artiwishing was
REALLY out of the question now.  The lava levels were a lot of fun,
though you always knew when you'd reached a demon lair because they
look completely different.  There were lots of footrices, so Asmodeus
fell to a rubber chicken. Juiblex was a lot of fun, I suspect if I
hadn't had the presence of mind to use the silver dagger (couldn't hit
him with two-weap) it could've gone on for a LONG time.

With the power of magical eyes, I suspect Blindfoldless will become a
challenging unofficial conduct before too long.

Vlad's tower was very familiar, though some of the flipped levels
didn't quite meet up to create the tower effect (very minor gripe). I
got XL19 from a wraith corpse outside Vlad's door. Everything was
going well - right up to the point where Vlad wielded Lifestealer,
cursed my silver dagger (off-hand weapon), stunned me, and ported
around very skilfully while I couldn't.

He'd drained me to level 13 (and back to only skilled in dagger) in 3
rounds of combat.  Got him to HP:47(100) with a few whacks of my
longsword and he ported away to heal while I uncursed my dagger.
Finally managed to hit him with a /oLightning, and an obliging red
dragon zapped him with a blast of fire that I dodged, letting me
dispatch him with a silver stab.  By this time I was XL 9 and very
relieved to see him meet his demise.  That same red dragon then
flagrantly refused to respect E and took me down to 15HP.
And that's how I found out that blessed !oFH have an extra use in
Sporkhack.

An archon on the way back to lavaland was a brief temptation as I
still wasn't using an artifact weapon, but I had no way of taming it,
and I didn't fancy my chances against it right then, seeing as though
I was still XL13.  Opted for unburdening myself back at the stash
again instead, and pray, hoping for crowning (See Invisible seems to
come and go by some mysterious recipe that I haven't figured out yet
in Spork).  Unfortunately, I didn't get crowned.

An ogre had a /oDeath in lavaland. The same level had 1 mmf and 1 mf,
but neither left corpses. Int was still woeful, at 9.  Had a bit of a
chase up a few levels with Baalzebub, but got him in the end.  Rand
out of /oCold charges at DL38, had to push boulders across the lava to
create bridges.

Dived past Orcus and came back up at him with a rubber bird.  Managed
to get level-drained in melee with a vampire (I should really know by
know, shouldn't I?) Found a much needed lava-cooling /oCold on the way
past Rodney, which would help in not having to change armour on the
ascension run.  Briefly had a pet chickatrice from an egg that I was
lugging around, but it wouldn't 'port with me, so I left it on an
island in the lava on DL45.  Found the brazier on DL52, realised I
still hadn't come across =3DoLev, so went to the stash to polypile for
it.  Finally got two in the one zapping session, and headed down to
meet Rodney.

Realised I'd run out of ways to solidify water again (though with
=3DoLev, not sure why I felt the need to, come to think of it), so
wished up marker number 5. Wrote and read a scroll of earth, found out
it was the wrong tower, and promptly fell into the moat...  Luckily
the charging scroll I'd just made survived the splash, though my BoH,
helm and cloak were all greaseless now.

Proceeded through to the zoo anyway, thinking I'd head back up to
regrease myself before tackling Rodney. Stood in the door with a c
corpse bashing everything, then took a wand of wind to the heap of
statues. Most satisfying! Got as far as the moat around Rodney and
went back up to tidy stuff up, grease my helm, bag and cloak and
relearn what spells I could for the ascension run.

Cut into Rodney diagonally, zapped /oDeath twice, missed him twice.
He blasted me with cold and I fell into the water twice and only
barely dragged myself out.  The next zap killed him though, so I
grabbed the book and ran like buggery.  Did the invocation, managed to
plant a water square right under a gremlin by doing that: "Oh well,
we'll deal with that later..." down to Moloch's I went.  Grabbed a
robe I'd been hoping to get a LOT earlier, killed the high priest and
learnt create monster (!) from his personal library.

A 'trice was kind enough to leave a corpse in the sanctum so I had
persuasion power when it came to getting beasts out of my way on the
way up Gehennom.  Rodney came back on DL 49, and left me alone until
I'd left Gehennom after that.

A hill shaman summoned locusts around halfway up, which was a bit
scary. An umber hulk confused me on a bridge across lava and I almost
didn't notice, which could've been a disaster.  Could've sworn I'd
stuck my =3DoLev back on at Juiblex, but no - into the water I went,
blanking a load of scrolls in my BoH.  I'd never gone back to my can
of grease, had I? *headdesk*

A blessed !oGL in the VoTD got me up to XL20, finally higher than I'd
entered Vlad's on all those turns ago. Took a little time in the
castle to replace my lost scrolls. Wished up a final magic marker,
much to Kerio's bafflement on NAO.

Rodney came back on DL 25, tried a bit of a summonstorm, but I was
right by the upstair and got away. Warning was very useful here, as I
lacked see invisible once more, and Rodney appeared as a nice bright
pink 5 so I knew where he was.  He seems to have a touch of death
attack similar to Death now, draining max HP.  I sent him packing for
the third time after about 3 levels of being annoyed by him as I
continued to climb madly.  Got to my stash and grabbed the grease can,
and also re-read a +oRC for good measure.

Rodney fell to a /oDeath on the Plane of Earth, which held no
surprises.  Air had a scattering of clouds throughout, but I didn't
get hit by lightning, and raced through, and although three Es all
engulfed me one after another they couldn't really touch my 280HP and
-35AC.

A salamander grabbed me on Fire, but the grease worked its magic.
Genocided electric eels and kraken with a blessed scroll on Water, and
found the portal very quickly.
Went after famine on Astral (left altar), encountering a yellow dragon
with 250HP, amongst others. Didn't find the locusts all that
troublesome, but I made a point of mashing any priest npcs into the
ground as soon as I could to cut down on insect summonings.  What was
a bit scary was the Nazgul in the middle of Astral stunning me with
its scream every few turns.
The partial effects of MR and reflection mean that even with both,
your HP loss per turn can be substantial even when there's nothing all
that nasty beating you up - just priests and angels. I hit 39HP in the
two turns it took me to spot that I was in trouble and take a potion
out of my BoH.  It was all good though, as I had enough death and
teleport wand charges left to take care of everything that wandered
into my path. Turned out to be the wrong altar, but it was ok because
pestillence had wandered over towards Death and I got to the middle
altar without meeting him.  Got two bits for an ale, had a swig of
booze, and offered the amulet.

Goodbye, spontiff the demigod.

It feels good, and it was great fun!

Regards,
Spontiff

